READ (corrected): largest arc is BOUNDED BELOW (~0.003-0.005) while apex <= ~V* (the bounded/finite
regime), then the apex's fine forbidden arcs (spacing 1/(14V)) start subdividing each core arc and
the largest arc decays ~1/V. The CROSSOVER apex ~ V* coincides with kps's D~213 and the V* atlas
~234 -- the SAME constant in 3 framings (paper enumeration bound / Conj-7.1 D / project V*).
So Conjecture 7.1(13) splits cleanly at V*: [apex<=V*] direct long arc (finite check);
[apex>V*] PEEL the apex (equidistribution, Node-3) onto the bounded core's long arc (0.006).
